English translation (for convenience; the German version prevails)

1. Without separate permission you may
   a) view and review the source code,
   b) install and use the installation packages (.spk) published by the
      copyright holder on your own devices for private, non-commercial purposes,
   c) build and modify the source code for your own private, non-commercial use,
   d) fork the repository using GitHub's fork feature as far as GitHub's Terms
      of Service provide; a fork grants no further rights.

2. Without prior written permission of the copyright holder you may not
   a) distribute, publish or share the source code or installation packages –
      in whole, in part or modified – (sharing a link to this repository or its
      releases is allowed),
   b) use the software commercially, in particular sell, rent, offer it as a
      service or bundle it with paid products or services,
   c) remove or alter copyright, trademark or license notices.

3. Contributions (e.g. issues, pull requests, patches): by submitting a
   contribution you grant the copyright holder a non-exclusive, perpetual,
   worldwide, royalty-free right to use, modify and publish it within the
   project under this or any other license.

4. Third-party components are subject to their own licenses (see NOTICE.md),
   in particular hls.js (Apache License 2.0) and the interface description from
   mikespub/synology (MIT License). This license does not restrict the rights
   granted there.

5. The software is provided free of charge and "as is", without warranty. The
   copyright holder is liable only for intent and gross negligence; liability
   under product liability law and for injury to life, body or health remains
   unaffected.

6. Synology, DiskStation, DSM, Video Station and DS video are trademarks of
   Synology Inc. DS Video Revival is not a Synology product and is neither
   supported nor authorized by Synology.

7. The laws of the Federal Republic of Germany apply.
